<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i-1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assertion seems incorrect based on the intended specification. Let's correct it to properly reflect the behavior described in the comment:

The correct assertion should state that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point to the previous size of the vector, the element at position `i` in the updated vector is equal to the element at position `i-1` in the old vector.

Here is the corrected assert statement:
<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

